{"step_index":1356,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:50Z","thinking":"Initial hypothesis: The HTML form defines the parameters for a search query. The `action` attribute specifies the target URL for the search. Parameters like `search_area`, `search_state`, `search_kind`, `search_type`, and `search_word` likely control the search criteria.\n\nNext, I'll attempt to construct a URL based on the observed form structure. The parameters appear to be key-value pairs appended to the base URL. I will need to understand the meaning of each parameter value to construct a valid and meaningful search request.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"node -e \"\nconst https = require('https');\nconst iconv = require('util');\n\nconst url = 'https://book.mcst.go.kr/html/searchList.php?search_area=6260000&search_state=13&search_kind=&search_type=1&search_word=' + encodeURIComponent('도서출판일광');\n\nhttps.get(url, (res) => {\n  let chunks = [];\n  res.on('data', c => chunks.push(c));\n  res.on('end', () => {\n    const buf = Buffer.concat(chunks);\n    const html = buf.toString('utf-8');\n    console.log('Status:', res.statusCode, 'Length:', html.length);\n    // Print table or search results\n    const m = html.match(/<table[\\s\\S]*?<\\/table>/gi) || [];\n    console.log('Tables found:', m.length);\n    if (m.length > 0) {\n      console.log('Table snippet:', m[m.length - 1].slice(0, 1000));\n    }\n  });\n});\n\"","Cwd":"C:\\Users\\lg\\.gemini\\antigravity\\worktrees\\resilient-bardeen\\fill_missing_business_numbers","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Test MCST publisher search request","toolSummary":"Test MCST publisher search request"}}]}
